  "notes": "Apple MacBook Pro 2018, close up, 'multiple keystrokes, single clicks in different speeds' (khenshom: Sennheiser MKE600 on a Zoom H5), 53.1 s, 48 kHz mono, floor -84.6 dBFS (best of 23 keyboards), peak -2.5 dBFS (one loud press at 14.8 s; the other listed presses sit at -14..-35 dBFS, a spread of about 20 dB: normalise per press to within sigma 2 dB). 18 clean single presses by earshot find (event kind, none marked head cut / tail cut, heads -40..-53 dB, tails -29..-57 dB), listed in the earshot.trims. For ~SPACE / RETURN (deeper): the file does not label them; by low-band share (<400 Hz) and centroid the deepest presses are 26.366-26.680 (centroid 2.9 kHz, 34 % below 400 Hz, head -38 dB, tail -39 dB) and 4.313-4.421 (centroid 2.7 kHz, 44 %, but head -33 dB and short) then 24.339-24.565 and 35.391-35.540; I could not confirm which is a space bar or a return (no ears): audition 26.366-26.680 as 'return' and pitch a normal press -3 st for the chord's second key. The 14.8 s press (14.836-15.260) is the loudest press of the file (peak -2.5 dBFS, tail -57 dB): audition it as the return key. Preview is 110 kbps mono (the upload is mono). CC0.",
